# What `railway up` must NOT upload from backend/ (the upload root for api, worker and
# beat). The image's own build context is trimmed by .dockerignore; this file is about
# the tarball that crosses the wire — .venv alone is ~390 MB and is rebuilt in the
# image from uv.lock anyway, so leaving it out is the difference between a minute and
# ten. railway.json, Dockerfile, docker/, app/, migrations/, alembic.ini, pyproject.toml
# and uv.lock must all stay.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.storage/
logs/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
